{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.ReidemeisterMassInvariance","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.ReidemeisterMassInvariance","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":38,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:calibrated_mass_pos_of_borromeanQuark","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"calibrated_mass_pos_of_borromeanQuark","kind":"theorem","line":227,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/reidemeister-mass-invariance.lean#L227-L246","doc":"**Conditional consequence of `BorromeanQuark`** (per CLAUDE.md §3b-cond):\na volume-calibrated bare-mass functional is strictly positive on the\nphysical regime `q > 1`.\n\nNow genuinely conditional.  In the previous form the hypothesis was\nderivable, so this theorem — presented as a §3b-cond conditional result —\nheld unconditionally.\n\nNamed in the Mathlib `_of_` conditional-lemma style (§3b-cond): the\nconclusion (calibrated mass positive) `_of_` the hypothesis\n(`BorromeanQuark`, carried as the load-bearing `[·]` instance binder the\n§3b-cond banner audit keys on). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:not_borromeanQuark_const_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"not_borromeanQuark_const_zero","kind":"theorem","line":218,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/reidemeister-mass-invariance.lean#L218-L225","doc":"**The carrier is refutable**, which is the whole point of the parameter:\nthe constantly-zero functional is not volume-calibrated.  The previous\nexistential form admitted no refutation, because it quantified over the\nfunctional it was constraining. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:BorromeanQuark.volume_calibrates_mass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"BorromeanQuark.volume_calibrates_mass","kind":"theorem","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/reidemeister-mass-invariance.lean#L215-L215","doc":"Conjecture content (mirrors `borromean_quark.volume_calibrates_mass`):\nthe baryon bare-mass functional is calibrated by the Borromean hyperbolic\nvolume, i.e. at every `q > 1` it equals `borromeanVolume / (1 − 1/q)²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:BorromeanQuark.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"BorromeanQuark.mk","kind":"ctor","line":211,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/reidemeister-mass-invariance.lean#L211-L211","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:BorromeanQuark","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"BorromeanQuark","kind":"class","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/reidemeister-mass-invariance.lean#L174-L216","doc":"Local mirror of `conj:borromean-quark`'s axiomatised class, **parametrised\non the mass functional**.\n\n## Why the parameter, and what it fixes\n\nThis mirror previously read\n\n```lean\nclass BorromeanQuark : Prop where\n  volume_calibrates_mass :\n    ∃ (V : ℝ) (m : ℝ → ℝ), 0 < V ∧ ∀ q : ℝ, q > 1 → m q = V / (1 - 1 / q) ^ 2\n```\n\nand its docstring claimed *\"an instance must exhibit such a calibrated\nfunctional — not merely assert `True`.\"*  **That claim was false.**  Both\n`V` and `m` were existentially bound, with `m` defined from `V` by the very\nequation being asserted, so\n\n```lean\ninstance : BorromeanQuark := ⟨⟨1, fun q => 1 / (1 - 1/q)^2, one_pos, fun _ _ => rfl⟩⟩\n```\n\ntypechecks.  The carrier constrained nothing, and the downstream\n`[BorromeanQuark]`-conditional theorem was therefore unconditional.\n\nThe rule the old form broke: **a carrier whose constraining fields relate\nonly its own bound data is a definition of a structure, not a statement of\na conjecture.**  A conjecture is a claim about objects fixed elsewhere.  So\n`bareMass` is a *parameter* here, and the class says something about a\nfunctional it was handed — see `not_borromeanQuark_const_zero`, which\nrefutes it at a specific functional.  The old form admitted no such\nrefutation at all.\n\nMeasured across the corpus in\n`docs/audits/2026-09-04-self-satisfying-conjecture-carriers.md`: ten classes\nnamed `BorromeanQuark`, no two with the same fields, **all ten trivially\ninhabited**. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:borromeanVolume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"borromeanVolume","kind":"def","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/reidemeister-mass-invariance.lean#L168-L172","doc":"The hyperbolic volume of the Borromean complement, `Vol(S³ ∖ B₃)`.\nDeclared locally so the carrier below can pin the mass functional to a\nNAMED constant without a cross-module import (the canonical declaration is\n`QOU.Archimedean.borromean_volume`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:identity_preserved_by_shell_transition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"identity_preserved_by_shell_transition","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/reidemeister-mass-invariance.lean#L150-L153","doc":"The particle identity is unchanged by shell transitions. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:shell_advance","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"shell_advance","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/reidemeister-mass-invariance.lean#L141-L148","doc":"Shell transition: two R-I moves (writhe +2) advances shell by 1.\n(Stated over `Int` writhes; the archimedean shell-advance reading is\nnot meaningful over `R_q`, so it is recorded here as a `decide`-class\narithmetic identity on the concrete writhe ladder.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:first_excited_shell","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"first_excited_shell","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/reidemeister-mass-invariance.lean#L138-L139","doc":"First excited state has writhe 5, shell 2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:ground_state_shell","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"ground_state_shell","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/reidemeister-mass-invariance.lean#L135-L136","doc":"Ground state trefoil has writhe 3, shell 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:shellNumber","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"shellNumber","kind":"def","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/reidemeister-mass-invariance.lean#L132-L133","doc":"Shell number from writhe: n = (w - 1) / 2 for the trefoil. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:bindingEnergy_R1_changes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"bindingEnergy_R1_changes","kind":"axiom","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/reidemeister-mass-invariance.lean#L123-L126","doc":"Binding energy changes under R-I (shell transition). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:bindingEnergy_R3_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"bindingEnergy_R3_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/reidemeister-mass-invariance.lean#L117-L121","doc":"Binding energy is invariant under R-III — a corollary of\n`invariant_under_R3`, formerly `axiom bindingEnergy_R3_invariant`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:bindingEnergy_R2_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"bindingEnergy_R2_invariant","kind":"axiom","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/reidemeister-mass-invariance.lean#L113-L115","doc":"Binding energy is invariant under R-II and R-III. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:bindingEnergy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"bindingEnergy","kind":"axiom","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/reidemeister-mass-invariance.lean#L108-L111","doc":"Binding energy depends on the embedding (writhe-sensitive).\nIt is a regular isotopy invariant but not a knot invariant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:bareMass_R3_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"bareMass_R3_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/reidemeister-mass-invariance.lean#L103-L106","doc":"Bare mass is invariant under R-III — a corollary of `invariant_under_R3`,\nformerly `axiom bareMass_R3_invariant`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:bareMass_R2_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"bareMass_R2_invariant","kind":"axiom","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/reidemeister-mass-invariance.lean#L101-L101","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:bareMass_R1_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"bareMass_R1_invariant","kind":"axiom","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/reidemeister-mass-invariance.lean#L97-L99","doc":"Bare mass is a knot invariant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:invariant_under_R3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"invariant_under_R3","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/reidemeister-mass-invariance.lean#L89-L95","doc":"**R-III invariance is not a conjecture — it holds for every function.**\n`applyR3 K := K`, so `f (applyR3 K) = f K` is `rfl` whatever `f` is.  This\nwas two separate axioms (`bareMass_R3_invariant`, `bindingEnergy_R3_invariant`);\nboth were provable all along, and are now the single theorem below.  Nothing\nabout mass or binding energy is used. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:bareMass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"bareMass","kind":"axiom","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/reidemeister-mass-invariance.lean#L83-L87","doc":"Bare mass depends only on the knot type (hyperbolic volume).\nSince knot type is invariant under R-I, R-II, R-III,\nbare mass is a knot invariant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:writhe_R1_changes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"writhe_R1_changes","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/reidemeister-mass-invariance.lean#L75-L77","doc":"Writhe is NOT a knot invariant (R-I changes it). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:writhe_R3_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"writhe_R3_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/reidemeister-mass-invariance.lean#L72-L73","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:writhe_R2_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"writhe_R2_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/reidemeister-mass-invariance.lean#L68-L70","doc":"Writhe is a regular isotopy invariant (R-II, R-III). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:applyR3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"applyR3","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/reidemeister-mass-invariance.lean#L65-L66","doc":"R-III does not change writhe or crossing number. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:applyR2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"applyR2","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/reidemeister-mass-invariance.lean#L60-L63","doc":"R-II does not change writhe (adds two opposite crossings). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:applyR1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"applyR1","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/reidemeister-mass-invariance.lean#L54-L58","doc":"R-I changes writhe by ±1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:KnotDiagram.crossingNumber","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"KnotDiagram.crossingNumber","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/reidemeister-mass-invariance.lean#L52-L52","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:KnotDiagram.writhe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"KnotDiagram.writhe","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/reidemeister-mass-invariance.lean#L51-L51","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:KnotDiagram.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"KnotDiagram.mk","kind":"ctor","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/reidemeister-mass-invariance.lean#L50-L50","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:KnotDiagram","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"KnotDiagram","kind":"structure","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/reidemeister-mass-invariance.lean#L49-L52","doc":"Writhe of a knot diagram: sum of signed crossings. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:knot_invariant_is_regular","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"knot_invariant_is_regular","kind":"theorem","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/reidemeister-mass-invariance.lean#L40-L43","doc":"Every knot invariant is a regular isotopy invariant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:IsRegularInvariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"IsRegularInvariant","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/reidemeister-mass-invariance.lean#L36-L38","doc":"A regular isotopy invariant is unchanged by R-II and R-III only. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:IsKnotInvariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"IsKnotInvariant","kind":"def","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/reidemeister-mass-invariance.lean#L32-L34","doc":"A knot invariant is a function unchanged by all three moves. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:ReidemeisterMove.R3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"ReidemeisterMove.R3","kind":"ctor","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/reidemeister-mass-invariance.lean#L30-L30","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:ReidemeisterMove.R2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"ReidemeisterMove.R2","kind":"ctor","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/reidemeister-mass-invariance.lean#L29-L29","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:ReidemeisterMove.R1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"ReidemeisterMove.R1","kind":"ctor","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/reidemeister-mass-invariance.lean#L28-L28","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:ReidemeisterMove","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"ReidemeisterMove","kind":"inductive","line":26,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/reidemeister-mass-invariance.lean#L26-L30","doc":"The three Reidemeister moves on knot diagrams. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:R_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"R_q","kind":"def","line":22,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/reidemeister-mass-invariance.lean#L22-L22","signatureChunk":0}]}